# ── Lake Tahoe, west-shore slope above the lake ───────────────────────────────
# A real observation entered through the harness. Everything below is either
# read off the photograph or a documented inference; anything not directly
# observable is marked. Run:
#   ./gradlew ecologyExperiment -Pspec=docs/tahoe-westshore.eco

name: Tahoe west-shore montane conifer stand
keys: 120
seed: 2026
window: 200

# ── ABIOTIC ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Only four knobs exist. area/temperature/wind/distance are unitless multipliers
# in this engine, so each is a RATIO against a neutral lowland stand, not a
# measurement. Elevation, aspect and slope have no field at all -- see notes.
factor: area 0.6           # a slope bench, not a basin: less effective habitat
factor: temperature 0.75   # montane, ~6,800 ft: shorter season, slower rates
factor: wind 1.4           # open lake fetch to the east, exposed canopy
factor: distance 1.1       # ~15 km of open water to the far shore

# ── BIOTIC: canopy cover by taxon ────────────────────────────────────────────
# Photo-estimated crown cover, percent. NOT stem counts -- the engine has no
# cover field, so cover is entered in the count slot. See the gap note below.
data: canopy Abies_concolor=45 Pinus_jeffreyi=30 Calocedrus_decurrens=8 Pinus_lambertiana=5 Abies_magnifica=4 standing_dead=3

# Understory and ground layer, percent cover of the open bench in the foreground.
data: understory Arctostaphylos_patula=25 Chrysolepis_sempervirens=15 graminoids=30 forbs=10 bare_litter=20

# Structural elements present in frame, counted as occurrences.
data: structure canopy_gap=2 standing_snag=1 multi_layer_canopy=3 lake_edge_ecotone=1

# ── PHYLOGENY of the conifers recorded ───────────────────────────────────────
# Cupressaceae sister to Pinaceae; within Pinaceae, Pinus and Abies as clades.
tree: conifers (Calocedrus_decurrens,((Pinus_jeffreyi,Pinus_lambertiana),(Abies_concolor,Abies_magnifica)));

# ── THEORY ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The lake is a dispersal barrier: the Carson Range across the water is an
# island for anything that does not cross open water well.
model: island 0.35 0.12 90 0 60
# Stand density relaxing toward carrying capacity after the last disturbance.
model: logistic 0.09 400 40 80

# ── FIELD NOTEBOOK ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
note: clear sky, no cloud and no smoke -- deep unscattered blue to the horizon
note: sun high and shadows short -- near midday, and the lake is unruffled inshore
note: snow persists only on the highest north-facing benches of the far range
note: full leaf-out in the shrub layer and no snow at the viewpoint -- early summer
note: lake water reads deep blue with no green cast, consistent with an oligotrophic, low-productivity water column
note(canopy): two species carry the stand -- white fir and Jeffrey pine; the rest are scattered individuals
note(canopy): one grey standing snag mid-frame, crown intact, no foliage -- recent mortality, still holding branch structure
note(structure): the view corridor itself is a canopy gap; regeneration visible along its floor
note(understory): shrub layer is continuous on the open bench and absent under closed canopy -- a light-driven boundary
# --- INFORMATION THE HARNESS COULD NOT HOLD IN A FIELD, ONLY AS PROSE ---
note: NO FIELD -- coordinates, approximately 39.1 N, 120.1 W, west shore
note: NO FIELD -- elevation of viewpoint approximately 6,800 ft; lake surface 6,225 ft
note: NO FIELD -- aspect east-northeast, slope moderate, descending to the shore
note: NO FIELD -- date and observer of record
note: NO FIELD -- source photograph identifier
note: NO FIELD -- canopy cover entered as counts because there is no cover-class type
note: NO FIELD -- species identifications are photo-based and uncertain at the species level for Calocedrus, Pinus lambertiana and Abies magnifica

# ── HYPOTHESES, written before the run ───────────────────────────────────────
expect: richness(canopy) <= 6
expect: evenness(canopy) is uneven
expect: turnover(canopy, understory) is major
expect: shannon(understory) > 1.4
expect: evenness(structure) is very-even
